R e a d m e
-----------

Docked -> Preflight -> Takeoff -> Flight -> Approach -> Landing -> Docked

QUICK START
-----------

Load the script. It creates a complete, uncommented [stager] section in this
PB's Custom Data. The defaults work immediately when the landing PB is named
Spugs Auto Landing and its destination argument is default_home. Run preflight
to launch and approach to land.

DISPLAYS
-----------

Rename an LCD to include [stager]:
Bridge LCD [stager]

Rename a cockpit to include [stager]. Its largest screen is used automatically:
Main Cockpit [stager]

To choose another screen, put this in that cockpit's Custom Data, not the PB:
[stager]
display_surface=1

Screen numbers start at 0; display_surface=-1 automatically selects the largest.
Tag more LCDs or cockpits for more dashboards.
The dashboard shows stage, countdown, readiness and errors. Add status to a
light's name to give it the same colour as the dashboard square.

STAGES
-----------

Docked: recharge batteries; stockpile gas; disable reactors, hydrogen engines,
thrusters, gyros, dampeners, lights, ore detector, tools and weapons.
Preflight: enable flight power, thrust, gyros, dampeners and lights; stop gas
stockpiling; disable tools/weapons; check readiness.
Takeoff: disconnect ship connectors and unlock landing gear.
Flight: keep flight systems active. Unlisted equipment remains unchanged.
Approach: enable gear autolock, disable tools/weapons and run stow hooks.
Landing: call Spug once; a connector entering Connected immediately docks.

PB CONFIGURATION
-----------

All settings are added automatically without comments. Edit values in place.
auto_takeoff and auto_landing control timed transitions. Their delays default
to one second. readiness_threshold_percent applies to enabled battery and tank
checks. check_flight_systems also requires usable thrust and gyros.

Leave docking_connector blank to use all ship connectors, or enter one exact
name. landing_programmable_block and landing_argument configure Spug. Tags
select the status light and displays. Stage colours use R,G,B values.

Edits and deleted settings are detected on the next script update. Missing keys
are restored. Invalid values use their defaults and show a warning. Malformed
INI is left intact while the script uses defaults; fixing it resumes saving.
Use one key=value per line under [stager]. Other sections are preserved.
Timing/readiness/display changes apply live. Stage actions apply on entry or
retry, so editing Custom Data does not repeat hooks or disconnect the ship.

BLOCK OVERRIDES
-----------

Each ship block receives its own [stager] settings and blank stage overrides.
Blank actions inherit category/built-in defaults; ignore leaves it unchanged:
[stager]
docked=off
preflight=on
flight=ignore

Actions: on/off/ignore; battery auto/recharge/discharge; tank normal/stockpile;
controller dampeners_on/dampeners_off; connector connect/disconnect; gear
lock/unlock/autolock; door open/close; timer trigger/start/stop; PB run:<argument>.

managed=false excludes stage actions. readiness=false excludes its readiness
check. docking=false excludes a connector from dock detection and default
connector actions; explicit actions on that connector still run.

For solar mechanisms, put flight=trigger on a deploy timer and approach=trigger
on a separate stow timer. Hooks run once per stage and completed hooks are not
repeated by retry. Increase approach_delay_seconds to allow stowing to finish.

The blank <stage>.<category> entries in PB Custom Data inherit built-in actions.
Set one to override a category, such as docked.reactor=on.
Categories: battery, reactor, engine, thruster, gyro, controller, tank,
connector, gear, light, ore_detector, tool, weapon, door, timer, program, other.
Individual block actions take precedence.

COMMANDS
-----------

preflight / approach    Normal launch and landing controls.
stage <name>            Select any stage directly.
landing                 Start Landing now, skipping the Approach delay.
stage takeoff -force    Bypass readiness only.
pause / resume          Freeze/resume automatic transitions.
reload / retry          Reload config / retry failed actions.
status / help           Show current status or display this help message.
